From e51d4c05d2a865eeb3eb64596f72b5e071233937 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:08:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] perf(kanban): annotation + links refresh reuse
 untouched boards' slices; heartbeats move no content key

On hermes-hub the main board's activity revision bumped ~39x/min (18 of them heartbeat events) and both
background refreshers rebuilt every board's slice on each bump: kanban-annotation 11.1% and kanban-remote-links
9.4% of a core (t_01a1cb9d4cfc595b run2).

- kanban_activity_revision: the task_events insert trigger skips kind='heartbeat'. Its only reader is the
  card-details strip (latest event), which is read on every session_tasks call and never cached on this key.
  Run/task heartbeat stamps were already bookkeeping columns. An older writer's unconditional trigger keeps
  readers on a valid superset key (trigger names unchanged); this version's init repairs it.
- kanban_links_narrow: a published links entry records which local boards its origin rows read (project()'s
  observe_local_binding and _without_local_open_duplicates read only this origin's own rows' board). A current
  fingerprint differing only in the keys of boards it never read is still fresh. Hub replica, ledger, read
  boards and any new board must be equal; undeclared projectors and unreadable rows keep the exact fingerprint.
  TTL unchanged.
- attention pass: per (scope, board) memo of the recent-done read keyed on board_memo_key; a later cut-off only
  filters rows. Busy/unknown keys never match.

Synthetic benchmark (scripts/benchmark_kanban_annotation_poll.py, 14 boards, 1 heartbeat/s, a commit every
30 s, 3 s polls past TTLs): 57-63 ms -> 8-9 ms CPU per poll; projections 40 -> 0, recent-done reads 560 -> 4,
count reads 40 -> 4 over 40 polls.

Refs: t_01a1cee98aaa8db1
